  "narrative": "No new validation results or response deadlines were released at this synthesis step, and no new validation request is possible because the validation budget is exhausted. I therefore made no accept/reject changes and only closed active investigations for final reporting. \n\nFinal scientific report. Direction convention used throughout: for direction -1, a positive signed estimate means the exposed group has a lower numeric dependency_composite, i.e. stronger measured dependency; for direction +1, a positive signed estimate means a higher numeric dependency_composite, i.e. weaker measured dependency or a claimed amplification of that contrast. More negative numeric scores mean stronger dependency. The outcome-specific threshold was 0.15 composite dependency-score units in the claimed direction. Because many subgroup and interaction contrasts were tested, repeated overlapping subgroup results are robustness checks, not independent replication. All conclusions are dataset-specific associations among measured predictors, constructed assays, and the composite endpoint; they do not establish causality, mechanism, gene or pathway roles, clinical meaning, or generalizability.\n\nSupported robust findings. KEAP1 loss is robustly associated with a higher numeric dependency_composite, meaning weaker measured dependency. The main contrast has discovery signed estimate +0.810 with lower bound +0.745 R6 and independent validation signed estimate +0.846 with lower bound +0.755 R13. The association survives across Kras mutation status R164 and R165, TP53-loss and TP53-intact backgrounds R15 and R14, SMARCA4-loss and SMARCA4-intact backgrounds R49 and R50, PTEN-loss and triple-loss backgrounds R189 and R54, adenocarcinoma R152, and research_signature bands R227 and R230. Tested interactions do not certify meaningful modification by Kras R11, ploidy R35, mutation burden R37, research_signature_a R63 and R224, research_signature_b R143 and R222, or lineage subtype R237. \n\nTP53 loss is likewise robustly associated with higher numeric score, meaning weaker measured dependency. Discovery signed estimate +0.829 lower +0.767 R4 and validation signed estimate +0.821 lower +0.739 R26. Contextual robustness includes Kras mutant R166, Kras wild-type R167, KEAP1-loss and KEAP1-intact backgrounds R17 and R16, SMARCA4-loss and SMARCA4-intact backgrounds R51 and R52, PTEN-loss and triple-loss backgrounds R190 and R55, adenocarcinoma R153, research_signature_a R228, and research_signature_b bands R231 and R219. Interaction tests are generally null, including Kras R10, ploidy R36 with validation R106, mutation burden R38, cas9 activity R23, lineage subtype R238, and research signatures R64, R118, R159, R203, and R223. \n\nSMARCA4 loss is robustly associated with lower numeric score, meaning stronger measured dependency. Reversed main effect R28 signed +0.804 lower +0.742 and validation R39 signed +0.796 lower +0.703. Contextual robustness includes TP53-loss and TP53-intact R42 and R41, KEAP1-loss and KEAP1-intact R44 and R43, PTEN-loss and triple-loss R191 and R56, adenocarcinoma R201, research_signature bands R214 and R232, and upper research_signature_b R217. Interactions are null: TP53 R67, KEAP1 R68, research_signature_a R65 and R109, research_signature_b R117 and R130, and aneuploidy R202. \n\nMSI-high is strongly associated with lower numeric score, meaning stronger measured dependency, but remains discovery-supported and independently unvalidated because validation budget is exhausted. Main contrast R179 signed +0.775 lower +0.664. Contextual lower bounds generally remain above threshold: adenocarcinoma R194 lower +0.611, triple-loss-free R211 lower +0.666, high mutation burden R212 lower +0.583, PTEN-intact R213 lower +0.686, research_signature_a high R229 lower +0.637, research_signature_b upper R220 lower +0.456, and research_signature_b median-upper R233 lower +0.525. Interaction tests with research_signature_a R192, research_signature_b R193, and aneuploidy R195 are not meaningful. The small exposed cells make validation especially valuable if future budget exists. \n\nPTEN loss is the main context-dependent finding. The broad average lower-score association is accepted but borderline: R33 signed +0.239 lower +0.145 and validation R53 signed +0.285 lower +0.146. Because both lower bounds are just below 0.15, the broad effect should be described as weak or borderline rather than robust. Stronger PTEN-lower-score associations occur when research_signature_a is median-or-high and research_signature_b is low or low-to-median. Validated examples are triple-loss-free PTEN R57 with validation R66 lower +0.178, and triple-loss-free with high research_signature_a and low research_signature_b R120 with validation R132 lower +0.581. Discovery-supported examples include all-sample high research_signature_a and low research_signature_b R123 lower +0.626, high research_signature_a and low-to-upper research_signature_b R210 lower +0.498, high research_signature_a and low-to-median research_signature_b R138 lower +0.661, adenocarcinoma high-research_signature_a low-research_signature_b R160 lower +0.499, TP53-loss-free R182 lower +0.503, KEAP1-loss-free R183 lower +0.492, and SMARCA4-loss-free R184 lower +0.520. These co-loss-free contexts argue that the effect is not driven by one single co-occurring loss, though they are not independent validations. \n\nResearch-signature modification of PTEN loss is asymmetric. Higher research_signature_a amplifies the PTEN-lower-score contrast, with R99 signed +0.540 lower +0.364 and validation R105 lower +0.242; high-research_signature_a triple-loss contrast R110 signed +0.557 lower +0.423 and validation R119 lower +0.323; and TP53-loss-free high-research_signature_a interaction R188 lower +0.440. Higher research_signature_b attenuates the PTEN-lower-score contrast. Broad attenuation R77 signed +0.423 lower +0.216 but validation R92 lower only +0.133, so this is discovery-supported rather than fully independently threshold-certified. The upper research_signature_b interaction in a median-or-high research_signature_a background R141 lower +0.353 is accepted as discovery-supported. Importantly, high research_signature_b is not a globally attenuating environment: SMARCA4 loss R217 lower +0.710, KEAP1 loss R218 lower +0.720, TP53 loss R219 lower +0.616, and MSI-high R220 lower +0.456 remain threshold-supported in that band. \n\nA narrower PTEN research_signature boundary was discovery-supported: all-sample high research_signature_a with median-to-upper research_signature_b R137 lower +0.178, and the corresponding interaction with median-or-high research_signature_a R156 lower +0.156. However, wider high research_signature_b boundaries remained unresolved: triple-loss high-research_signature_a high-research_signature_b discovery R121 lower +0.159 failed validation R145 lower +0.069; TP53-loss-free median-to-upper R205 lower +0.135; interaction median-to-upper with median research_signature_a R209 lower +0.146; several related lower bounds were +0.018, +0.021, +0.024, +0.026, +0.030, +0.064, or below zero. Several clean triple-loss or small-band intersections had invalid cells. \n\nNegative findings. The constructed research markers D, E, and F have no meaningful main effects or pairwise interactions: R1, R2, R3, R8, R9. KRAS is not a meaningful main effect R5 and does not certify modification of TP53 or KEAP1 effects R10 and R11. MYC amplification is not meaningful overall R88, in TP53-loss interaction R12, or in the four-loss-free background R89. EGFR R226, BRAF R225, ERBB2 R177, and their adenocarcinoma tests R154, R155, and R131 are null or subthreshold. Many other genomic predictors are null, opposite the claimed direction, or underpowered: STK11 R27, ARID1A R29, MTAP R30, CDKN2A broad R31, PIK3CA R32, RB1 R34, NF1 R91, SMAD4 R90, BRCA2 R178. Broad technical and culture predictors do not support meaningful dataset-specific effects: screen batch R19 and R20, CRISPR library R21, omics/QC completeness R104, R234, and R235, media serum contrasts R7, R175, and R236, and sex R176. Tested modifiers of robust dependencies generally failed. These are failures to support threshold effects in this dataset, not evidence of universal biological absence. \n\nUnresolved uncertainty. The main unresolved area is the PTEN-loss boundary where research_signature_b is above its median but below or near its upper quartile, especially with research_signature_a high and with co-loss restrictions. Some accepted lower bounds near +0.15 to +0.18 are discovery-supported but not independently validated, and overlapping variants often disagree. The exact boundary may be real but smaller than the strong signature-amplified or signature-attenuated contrasts. MSI-high is also unresolved only in the sense of lacking independent validation, not because its discovery effect is weak. Multiplicity, overlapping subgroup selection, and absence of true held-out discovery validation remain limitations. \n\nMost informative next analysis. If validation budget were restored, the highest-value validations are MSI-high R179 and the PTEN-loss research_signature_a-high/research_signature_b median-upper boundary claims represented by R137 and R156. If only discovery analysis is possible, the remaining best step is not another broad genomic or clinical main effect and not more overlapping PTEN signature variants; it is a pre-specified adequately powered non-overlapping PTEN boundary test with a fixed signature band and a planned independent validation. Since no validation can be requested now and further discovery would mostly multiply testing on the same boundary, I registered no new proposal in this final synthesis. All statements remain dataset-specific associations.",
  "research_notes": "FINAL. No new validation or due assessments; validation budget exhausted. Closed active claims without changing status. Direction: -1 positive signed estimate means lower numeric dependency_composite/stronger dependency; +1 positive means higher numeric score/weaker dependency. Threshold: signed lower bound > +0.15. All statements are dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable.\n\nRobust supported findings: KEAP1 loss higher score, validated R6 lower +0.745 and R13 lower +0.755. TP53 loss higher score, validated R4 lower +0.767 and R26 lower +0.739. SMARCA4 loss lower score, validated R28 lower +0.742 and R39 lower +0.703. MSI-high lower score, discovery-supported R179 lower +0.664 but unvalidated.\n\nPTEN loss is broad borderline R33 lower +0.145 and validation R53 lower +0.146, but context-dependent. Strong lower-score PTEN effects occur with high research_signature_a and low/low-mid research_signature_b: triple-loss R57 validation R66 lower +0.178; triple-loss sig_a-high sig_b-low R120 validation R132 lower +0.581. Discovery examples: all-sample sig_a-high sig_b-low R123 lower +0.626; sig_a-high sig_b-low-to-upper R210 lower +0.498; sig_a-high sig_b-low-to-median R138 lower +0.661; TP53-loss-free R182 lower +0.503; KEAP1-loss-free R183 lower +0.492; SMARCA4-loss-free R184 lower +0.520; adenocarcinoma R160 lower +0.499.\n\nSignature interaction asymmetry: research_signature_a amplifies PTEN lower-score contrast, validated interactions R99/R105 lower +0.242 and R110/R119 lower +0.323. research_signature_b attenuates PTEN lower-score contrast, broad R77 validation R92 lower only +0.133, upper-band R141 lower +0.353. High sig_b is not globally attenuating: SMARCA4 R217, KEAP1 R218, TP53 R219, MSI-high R220 remain threshold-supported.\n\nUnresolved PTEN boundary: median-to-upper sig_b with high sig_a discovery-supported R137 lower +0.178 and interaction R156 lower +0.156, but wider boundary fails or is underpowered: R121 validation R145 lower +0.069, R205 lower +0.135, R209 lower +0.146, R136 lower +0.136, R181 lower +0.026, R173 lower +0.024, R174 lower +0.030, R208 lower +0.064, R149 lower +0.018, R122 lower +0.021, R204 lower -0.036.\n\nNegative findings: research markers D/E/F and pairwise interactions R1-R3 R8 R9; KRAS R5 R10 R11; MYC R88 R12 R89; EGFR R226 R154; BRAF R225 R155; ERBB2 R177 R131; STK11 R27; ARID1A R29; MTAP R30; CDKN2A broad R31; PIK3CA R32; RB1 R34; NF1 R91; SMAD4 R90; BRCA2 R178. Technical predictors null: batch R19 R20, library R21, QC/omics R104 R234 R235, media R7 R175 R236, sex R176.\n\nNext if validation restored: validate MSI-high R179 and PTEN sig_a-high sig_b median-upper boundary R137/R156. Avoid more overlapping PTEN discovery variants. No new proposal registered because validation cannot be requested and additional discovery would mostly increase multiplicity."
